/**
 * CWE vs. CVE, in Stephen's wording of 2026-10-03, shown on /ai-news/cwes/
 * and on the Application and Product Security page beside the CWE table.
 */
---
<aside class="cwe-vs-cve">
  <p class="cvc-label">CWE vs. CVE</p>
  <p class="cvc-lead">A CWE describes an underlying software flaw or weakness type in the abstract,
    whereas a CVE identifies a distinct, specific instance of a vulnerability in a particular product.</p>
  <p>CWE is a dictionary of types of mistakes, like a blueprint for a bug. CVE is a registry of specific
    occurrences of a bug in real-world software, like Log4j or a specific iOS version.</p>
</aside>

<style>
  .cwe-vs-cve { background: #FFF6EC; border: 1px solid #F0D6B0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 1.4em 0; max-width: 780px; }
  .cvc-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #F07800; margin: 0 0 .5em; }
  .cvc-lead { font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.08rem; color: #201868; margin: 0 0 .6em; }
  .cwe-vs-cve p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; color: #3d3d46; }
</style>
